<!--
    kuna option bejoin (default callers) and option bejoinpass (default
    whole), GH-904 and GH-815: three more kinds of evidence that a big-endian
    register pair is one 64-bit value, each from a shape that printed a wrong
    value.

    -O0 reloads (bejoin_spill_ppc32_O0.o, bejoin_spill_sparc32_O0.o): clang
    -O0 spills an argument across a call and reloads it into the second
    return register before it sign-extends it into the first (`stw
    r3,8(r31); bl ext; lwz r4,8(r31); srawi r3,r4,31`), and keeps
    `long long t = x;` in two frame slots it reloads to return.  The reload
    was taken for a load, which is no extension, so widen printed `int
    widen` returning `a0 >> 0x1f`, uwiden `(uint8)a0 << 0x20` and local its
    halves swapped.  A reload of a frame slot is now the value stored there.
    local_hi and sign are the `int`s over the same values and stay `int`.

    A pair passed straight on (bejoin_handoff_ppc32_O2.o): to_dbl is `bl
    add64; bl __floatundidf`, which reads add64's two registers as its 64-bit
    argument; a call is not otherwise a read, so add64 printed its halves
    swapped.  A call to a compiler-runtime routine whose first parameter is a
    64-bit integer now reads the pair.

    Reloads that are no return (bejoin_discard_sparc32_O0.o,
    _mips32_O1.o): keep builds `long long t = y;` from a reloaded argument
    in %i0:%i1, stores it with `std %i0` and returns nothing; drop reloads a
    discarded `volatile long long` into $2:$3, then sets $2 to the 0 it
    returns.  The std reads both words and the overwritten load was never
    read, so neither proves a 64-bit return.

    A wrapper's sign test (bejoin_handoff_ppc32_O2.o, _mips32_O2.o): under
    bejoinpass whole wrap returns sum's whole value, but sign_of, which reads
    only wrap's first register, read it as wrap's low word, `(int4)wrap(..)`.
    A function that hands back a proven callee's pair is now proven itself
    under whole, so the read is the value's high word.

    Stage: P4 calls and prototypes (return recovery), options bejoin and
    bejoinpass.  Pass 1 is the default; pass 2 sets bejoin off (the reloads),
    bejoin evidence (the routine call) or bejoinpass off (the sign test).

    Images: decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/bejoin_spill_*.o
    from bejoin_spill.c, bejoin_handoff_*.o from bejoin_handoff.c,
    bejoin_discard_*.o from bejoin_discard.c; see bejoin_residue.provenance.
-->
